COMMITTEE OF THE WHOLE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Committee of the Whoie was held on Wednesday, November 20. 2024, in
Council Chambers and via electronic meeting, stalling at 6:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as
follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS:
President Ken Esquibel, Chairman; Dr. Michelle Aldrich; Bryan
Cook; Richard Johnson; Pete Laybourn; Scott Roybal; Tom Segrave; and Jeff White (via Zoom).
Absent: Dr. Mark Rinne
r
srt-yse7zr-r
-rra
AGENDA ITEMS
17.
ORDINANCE 2td READING
— Amending Section 8.60.080, Non-Compliant Vehicles as
a Nuisance, of the Municipal Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, declaring oversized
vehicles as a nuisance, providing for their regulation, clarifying provisions and making
conforming amendments. (SPONSORS
- DR. ALDRICH AND MR. JOHNSON)
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 2” reading, seconded by Mr. Johnson. Dr. Aldrich moved to
amend section 8.60.080 B (1) to remove “seventy-two (72) hours” and replace it with “five (5)
days,” seconded by Mr. Segrave. Motion to amend failed, in a tie vote, with President Esquibel
and committee members Cook, Johnson, and Layboum voting “NO” and Aldrich, Roybal,
Segrave, and White voting “YES.” Main motion carried with all members voting “YES” with the
exception of Laybourn who voted “NO.”
Ward III Councilwoman, Dr. Michelle Aldrich, and co-sponsor of the proposed ordinance
provided an overview and noted various complaints she’s received during her time in office.
Captain David Janes, Police Department, provided information related to the enforcement of the
proposed ordinance.
Eric Fountain, Compliance Director, and Anthony Bannon, Compliance
Department, provided information related to the department’s ability to provide adequate
enforcement.
President Esquibel and committee members Cook, Johnson, Layboum, Roybal,
Segrave, and White commented on the item.
Public comments were made by Gary Harley and
Alan Sheldon.
