a user fee for necessary funding and repealing obsolete provisions.
(SPONSOR
— MR.
JOHNSON)
Mr. Laybourn moved to approve on 2 reading, seconded by Mr. Roybal. Mr. Laybourn moved
to amend by substitute dated November 19, 2024, seconded by Mr. Roybal.
Motion to amend
carried by unanimous voice vote.
Main motion, as amended, carried with all members voting
“YES” with the exception of Aldrich who voted “NO.”
