### Page 2 of 2

```text
Ward I Councilman, Pete Laybourn, provided an introduction and brief history of the efforts to
develop the proposed ordinance. Tom Cobb, City Engineer, and Wes Bay, Stonmvater Division
Manager, provided a presentation on the proposed ordinance. Engineer Cobb provided substitutes
for both item #18 and #19 and noted the substitutes replace (in both documents) the term
“impervious area” with “hard surface” as the metric through which property is evaluated for the
imposition of the fee. Stefanie Boster, City Attorney, provided information related to communities
that have failed to properly manage stormwater programs.
President Esquibel and committee
members Aldrich, Cook, Johnson. Roybal, and Segrave commented on the item.
Committee
members Aldrich and Johnson thanked Councilman Laybourn for his extensive efforts on the
proposed Stormwater Runoff Management System.
19.
ORDINANCE _2nd READING
— Specifying the monthly Stormwater Runoff Management
System User Fee in accordance with Section 13.32.050 of the Municipal Code of the City
of Cheyenne, Wyoming. (SPONSOR— MR. JOHNSON)
Mr. Laybourn moved to approve on 2t’ reading, seconded by Mr. Segrave. Mr. Layboum moved
to amend by substitute dated November 19, 2024, seconded by Mr. Segrave.
Motion to amend
carried by unanimous voice vote.
Main motion, as amended, carried with all members voting
“YES” with the exception of Aldrich who voted “NO.”
Ward I Councilman, Pete Laybourn, advised the proposed ordinance authorizes the collection of a
fee associated with the creation of a Stormwater Runoff Management System and Tom Cobb, City
Engineer, provided additional information.
John Brodie, Deputy City Attorney, provided
information related to the accounting mechanism identified in the ordinance for the funds
collected. Committee members Aldrich. Roybal, and Segrave commented on the item. Committee
member White extended a thank you to Councilman Laybourn for his efforts on the proposed
Stormwater Runoff Management System.
There being no further items for the agenda to come before the Committee of the Whole, the
meeting was adjourned at 7:57 p.m.
Submitted by,
